  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e32879ae-fdb4-425f-a738-362e13939800",
    "name": "Partner Event Notifications API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "Event Notifications (also known as webhooks or postbacks) are HTTP requests that **impact.com sends to your server** in real time when relevant events occur — actions tracked, clicks credited, status changes, and so on.\n\nThis is an **inbound** integration: you configure a URL in your impact.com account, and impact.com fires HTTP requests at that URL when events happen. You don't call any impact.com endpoint to receive notifications.\n\n**How it works:**\n\n1. In your impact.com partner account, configure an Event Notification URL.\n2. Use placeholder tokens like `{CampaignId}`, `{ActionId}`, `{Status}`, `{Payout}` in either the URL (for GET delivery) or the JSON request body (for POST delivery). impact.com substitutes the real values at fire time.\n3. impact.com calls your URL whenever a matching event occurs.\n4. Your server returns a `2xx` response to acknowledge receipt. Non-`2xx` responses are retried by impact.com.\n\nThis spec documents the **shape of the request impact.com sends to your server** — it is not an endpoint you call.\n\n\nContact Support:\n Name: impact.com Developer Support",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
